    "comparisons": [
      {
        "name": "HEFA",
        "product": "加氢处理酯和脂肪酸（HEFA）工艺",
        "scenario": "将废弃食用油和其他脂肪转化为可持续航空燃料",
        "target_customer": "可持续航空燃料生产商",
        "funding_summary": "",
        "core_difference": "HEFA依赖有限的废弃油脂原料，约占当前SAF产量的95%，原料供应限制其规模化；Neela的技术将更丰富的废弃物（食物垃圾、农业残余物、林业副产品）转化为与现有HEFA生产兼容的原料。",
        "evidence_refs": [
          {
            "source_id": "FISRC-d4882614e143350f",
            "quote": "Most sustainable aviation fuel is currently produced using hydroprocessed esters and fatty acids (HEFA), a process that converts waste cooking oils and other fats into fuel. While HEFA accounts for approximately 95% of current SAF production, the availability of suitable waste oils and fats limits how far the technology can scale.",
